IMPORT prelude

-- A New Tax System (Family Assistance) Act 1999 (Cth) -- the immunisation requirements (s 6) and what failing them does to
-- Family Tax Benefit (s 61B; Sch 1 cll 7(2), (3), 26(3), (4)) and to the Child Care Subsidy (s 85BA(1)(a)(iii)); eligibility
-- for Family Tax Benefit and who is an FTB child (ss 21, 22, 26); the Part A income test (Sch 1 cll 1(2), 3, 25, 25D, 28, 38L-38N);
-- the newborn supplement (Sch 1 cl 35A) and the newborn upfront payment (s 58AA); and the Child Care Subsidy percentage, hourly
-- rate and subsidised hours (Sch 2 cll 2, 3, 11, 12).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 124, compilation date 1 July 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 73, 2025), register id
-- C2026C00331, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00490.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0004 in ../../../requirements.jsonl (priority 1), raised 9 times by the three Western Australian
-- cradle-to-grave lives: chloe c003, c064, c065, c066, c071; jake k002, k054; daniel d002, d040. SCOPED to the questions those
-- events ask: what immunisation status does to family assistance; what a newborn brings (newborn upfront payment, newborn
-- supplement, FTB Part A on the family income test); the Child Care Subsidy percentage and activity test; and whether a child born
-- outside marriage gets the same. The connected definitions, conditions and exceptions are added where the answer needs them.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. FTB Part B; maintenance income test (Sch 1 Div 5); rent assistance, energy supplement, FTB advances, multiple birth
-- allowance; the health check reduction (s 61A); percentage-of-care determinations and shared care (ss 35A-35T, Sch 1 cll 11, 27);
-- blended families (ss 27-29); stillborn baby payment; additional child care subsidy; the higher rate child percentage (Sch 2 cll
-- 3A, 3B); Schedule 3 (adjusted taxable income) and Schedule 4 (indexation) beyond the fact of indexation; residence beyond a flag.
-- The 1996 and 2006 events (daniel d002, jake k002) are not answerable from this compilation: see NOTES.md.
--
-- AMOUNTS ARE INPUTS. Every dollar amount in Schedules 1 and 2 used here is listed in Schedule 4 cl 2 as indexed, and Sch 2 cl 2(3)
-- says its printed caps "reflect the indexation applied on 1 July 2019". The printed figures are therefore not the figures paid in
-- 2030. Rules below take the amounts as parameters; the printed figure is quoted in the comment. The taper formulas in Sch 2 cl 3(2)
-- and the newborn supplement formulas in Sch 1 cl 35B(1) are absent from the deposit (the text reads "using the formula:" and stops),
-- so those results are inputs too.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `A New Tax System (Family Assistance) Act 1999 -- families`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `a` GREATER THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS
    IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the positive part of` MEANS
    IF `x` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `x` ELSE 0

§§ `6 -- the immunisation requirements`

-- s 6(1): when a child "meets the immunisation requirements" for CCS eligibility (Div 2 of Part 4A), ACCS (child wellbeing), and
-- the FTB child rate reduction under Sch 1 cl 7(2), (3), 26(3), (4) (ss 61A, 61B).
-- (2) "The child meets the immunisation requirements if the child has been immunised" -- s 3: immunised in accordance with a
-- standard or catch up vaccination schedule determined under s 4.
-- (3) certified medical contraindication; certified natural immunity; participant in an approved vaccine study.
-- (4) vaccine temporarily unavailable (Chief Medical Officer's certificate; Secretary satisfied the child would have been immunised;
-- the vaccine has not become available).
-- (5) vaccinated overseas, certified equivalent, and all other vaccinations received.
-- (6) the Secretary determines in writing that the child meets them.
-- There is no other ground. In particular the section has no exemption for a parent's conscientious or religious objection.
DECLARE `Immunisation facts` HAS
    `immunised under a standard or catch up schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
    `medical contraindication certified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `natural immunity certified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in an approved vaccine study` IS A BOOLEAN
    `vaccine temporarily unavailable as s 6(4) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `vaccinated overseas as s 6(5) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary has determined it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parent objects to vaccination` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the child` IS AN `Immunisation facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child meets the immunisation requirements` IF
        `the child`'s `immunised under a standard or catch up schedule`
    OR  `the child`'s `medical contraindication certified`
    OR  `the child`'s `natural immunity certified`
    OR  `the child`'s `in an approved vaccine study`
    OR  `the child`'s `vaccine temporarily unavailable as s 6(4) requires`
    OR  `the child`'s `vaccinated overseas as s 6(5) requires`
    OR  `the child`'s `the Secretary has determined it`

§§ `61B and Sch 1 cl 7(2) -- the FTB child rate reduction`

-- s 61B(1): the FTB child rate is reduced if the child does not meet the immunisation requirements "(ii) for family tax benefit paid
-- to the individual in instalments--before the end of the grace period".
-- (3) when the Secretary becomes aware, the Secretary "must give a notice"; (4) the grace period "(a) begins on the day specified as
-- the date of the notice ... and (b) ends 63 days after that day".
-- (2) the FTB child rate reduction period "(a) begin[s] on the day specified as the date of the notice ... and (b) end[s] on the day
-- the child meets the immunisation requirements". So once the grace period is missed, the reduction runs from the NOTICE date,
-- not from the end of the grace period.
-- Sch 1 cl 7(2): "the annual FTB child rate in relation to the child is reduced by $737.30 for each day in the FTB child rate
-- reduction period" (Method 2: cl 26(3), same figure). cl 7(3): for a past-period claim, reduced by $737.30 (once).
-- s 61C: nil, not negative -- the floor at nil below is an inference from s 61C's "rate ... is nil as a result of section 61A or
-- 61B". Meeting the requirements ON day 63 is treated as within the grace period (an inference: "ends 63 days after that day").
GIVEN `met the requirements` IS A BOOLEAN, `days after the notice date when met` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instalment FTB child rate is reduced` IF
    NOT (`met the requirements` AND `days after the notice date when met` AT MOST 63)

GIVEN `met the requirements` IS A BOOLEAN, `days after the notice date when met` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in the reduction period` MEANS
    IF `the instalment FTB child rate is reduced` `met the requirements` `days after the notice date when met`
    THEN `days after the notice date when met`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `annual FTB child rate` IS A NUMBER, `reduction amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the annual FTB child rate on a day in the reduction period` MEANS
    `the positive part of` (`annual FTB child rate` MINUS `reduction amount`)

§§ `85BA -- eligibility for the Child Care Subsidy`

-- s 85BA(1): eligible for CCS for a session of care if (a) at the time (i) the child is an FTB child, or a regular care child, of the
-- individual or partner; (ii) "the child is 13 or under and does not attend secondary school" (or a prescribed class); (iii) "the
-- child meets the immunisation requirements in section 6"; (iv) the individual or partner meets the residency requirements in
-- s 85BB; (b) a liability to pay for the session "under a complying written arrangement"; (c) the session is provided in Australia,
-- not part of the compulsory education program, and not in prescribed circumstances; (d) Division 5 does not prevent it; (e) any
-- prescribed requirements for the kind of service. Paragraphs (c)(iii), (d) and (e) are taken as satisfied here.
-- Contrast with FTB: an unimmunised child REDUCES the FTB child rate (s 61B) but REMOVES CCS eligibility altogether.
DECLARE `CCS session facts` HAS
    `FTB or regular care child of the individual or partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `child is 13 or under and not at secondary school` IS A BOOLEAN
    `child meets the immunisation requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `individual or partner meets the residency requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `liability under a complying written arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provided in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `part of the compulsory education program` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the session` IS A `CCS session facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is eligible for CCS for the session` IF
        `the session`'s `FTB or regular care child of the individual or partner`
    AND `the session`'s `child is 13 or under and not at secondary school`
    AND `the session`'s `child meets the immunisation requirements`
    AND `the session`'s `individual or partner meets the residency requirements`
    AND `the session`'s `liability under a complying written arrangement`
    AND `the session`'s `provided in Australia`
    AND (NOT `the session`'s `part of the compulsory education program`)

§§ `21, 22, 26 -- eligibility for Family Tax Benefit`

-- s 22(2): an individual is an FTB child of the adult if (a) "aged under 16"; (b) "in the adult's care"; (c) an Australian resident,
-- special category visa holder residing in Australia, or living with the adult; (d) legal responsibility as in (5)(a), (b) or (c):
-- the adult is legally responsible (alone or jointly) for day-to-day care, welfare and development; or a family law order or
-- parenting plan says the child is to live or spend time with the adult; or no one with legal responsibility has the child.
-- s 21(1): eligible if (a) at least one FTB child; (b) the individual is an Australian resident (or listed visa holder); (c) the
-- rate, worked out under Div 1 of Part 4 (with some reductions disregarded), "is greater than nil".
-- Nothing in ss 21 or 22 asks whether the parents are married, or whether the child was born within a marriage.
-- s 26(1): where 2 members of a couple would both be eligible "only one member is eligible" -- the one the Secretary determines,
-- having regard to who is primary carer and any written nomination. "member of a couple" has "the same meaning as in the Social
-- Security Act 1991" (s 3), which is not deposited in this row.
DECLARE `FTB facts` HAS
    `child age in years` IS A NUMBER
    `child is in the adult's care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `child is resident or lives with the adult` IS A BOOLEAN
    `adult has legal responsibility as s 22(5) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `adult is an Australian resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `rate would be greater than nil` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parents are married` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `f` IS AN `FTB facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child is an FTB child under s 22(2)` IF
        `f`'s `child age in years` LESS THAN 16
    AND `f`'s `child is in the adult's care`
    AND `f`'s `child is resident or lives with the adult`
    AND `f`'s `adult has legal responsibility as s 22(5) requires`

GIVEN `f` IS AN `FTB facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the adult is eligible for family tax benefit` IF
        `the child is an FTB child under s 22(2)` `f`
    AND `f`'s `adult is an Australian resident`
    AND `f`'s `rate would be greater than nil`

§§ `Sch 1 cll 1(2), 3, 25, 25D, 28, 38L-38N -- the Part A income test`

-- cl 1(2)(a): use Part 2 (Method 1) if the adjusted taxable income "does not exceed the individual's higher income free area", or
-- the individual or partner is receiving a social security pension or benefit (etc.); (b) otherwise Part 3 (Method 2).
-- cl 2: higher income free area -- printed basic amount $98,988 (indexed: Sch 4 cl 2 item 11). cl 38N: income free area $40,000
-- (indexed: item 13). s 3 / Sch 3 cl 3 note: for a member of a couple the adjusted taxable income includes the partner's.
-- cl 3 (Method 1): maximum rate (standard rate + newborn supplement + MBA + FTB Part A supplement + ...), less the income test
-- reduction (cl 38M: "20% of the income excess" over the income free area; cl 38L: nil for pension or benefit recipients), less
-- the maintenance reduction (not encoded); step 4: the Part A rate is that, or the base rate (cl 4: the Method 2 base rate) if
-- higher.
-- cl 25 (Method 2): Method 2 base rate, less cl 28 reduction "30% of the income excess" over the higher income free area = the
-- provisional Part A rate; step 3/cl 25D: the Method 2 income and maintenance tested rate = maximum rate less (20% of (HIFA - IFA)
-- plus 30% of (ATI - HIFA)); step 4: the Part A rate is the greater of the two.
-- Maintenance income is taken to be nil. The floor at nil is an inference (s 21(1)(c) speaks of a rate "greater than nil").
GIVEN `income` IS A NUMBER, `higher income free area` IS A NUMBER, `on a pension or benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part A is worked out by Method 1` IF
    `income` AT MOST `higher income free area` OR `on a pension or benefit`

GIVEN `maximum rate` IS A NUMBER, `Method 2 base rate` IS A NUMBER, `income` IS A NUMBER, `income free area` IS A NUMBER, `higher income free area` IS A NUMBER, `on a pension or benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Part A rate` MEANS
    IF `Part A is worked out by Method 1` `income` `higher income free area` `on a pension or benefit`
    THEN `the larger of`
            (IF `on a pension or benefit`
             THEN `maximum rate`
             ELSE `maximum rate` MINUS (`the positive part of` (`income` MINUS `income free area`) TIMES 20 DIVIDED BY 100))
            `Method 2 base rate`
    ELSE `the positive part of`
            (`the larger of`
                (`Method 2 base rate` MINUS ((`income` MINUS `higher income free area`) TIMES 30 DIVIDED BY 100))
                (`maximum rate` MINUS ((`higher income free area` MINUS `income free area`) TIMES 20 DIVIDED BY 100)
                                MINUS ((`income` MINUS `higher income free area`) TIMES 30 DIVIDED BY 100)))

§§ `Sch 1 cl 35A -- the newborn supplement`

-- cl 35A(1): newborn supplement is added, for a day, to the maximum rate (or Method 2 base rate) if subclause (2), (5) or (7)
-- applies. (2) parent of the child: (a) the individual or partner "is a parent of the child on that day"; (b) "the child is aged
-- less than one"; (c) the Part A rate would be greater than nil; (d) "that day occurs in the period of 13 weeks beginning on the
-- first day that paragraphs (a) to (c) are satisfied"; (e) the birth registration requirement is notified in time.
-- (8) "This clause does not apply, and is taken never to have applied, ... if parental leave pay is payable to the individual for
-- that child."
-- (9) Nor if parental leave pay is payable to another person "for a flexible PPL day for that child" and that person and the
-- individual "are members of a couple on that day".
-- (10) once added for 13 weeks to one member of a couple (no s 28/29 determination), the clause does not apply to the other member.
-- Only the parent route (2) is encoded; entrustment (5) and adoption (7) are not. "parental leave pay" and "flexible PPL day" have
-- the meanings in the Paid Parental Leave Act 2010, which is not deposited in this row. 13 weeks is counted as days 0 to 90 from
-- the first qualifying day (an inference about counting).
DECLARE `Newborn facts` HAS
    `individual or partner is a parent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `child is aged less than one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Part A rate would be greater than nil` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days since the first qualifying day` IS A NUMBER
    `birth registration notified in time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `parental leave pay payable to the individual for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `partner paid parental leave pay for a flexible PPL day while a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other member of the couple already had it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parents are married` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `n` IS A `Newborn facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `newborn supplement is added for the day` IF
        `n`'s `individual or partner is a parent`
    AND `n`'s `child is aged less than one`
    AND `n`'s `Part A rate would be greater than nil`
    AND `n`'s `days since the first qualifying day` AT LEAST 0
    AND `n`'s `days since the first qualifying day` LESS THAN 91
    AND `n`'s `birth registration notified in time`
    AND (NOT `n`'s `parental leave pay payable to the individual for the child`)
    AND (NOT `n`'s `partner paid parental leave pay for a flexible PPL day while a couple`)
    AND (NOT `n`'s `the other member of the couple already had it`)

§§ `58AA -- the newborn upfront payment`

-- s 58AA(1): "If, under Division 1A of Part 5 of Schedule 1, an amount of newborn supplement is added in relation to an individual
-- and an FTB child of the individual, then the individual is entitled to be paid, as an amount of family tax benefit, $500 in
-- respect of the FTB child." Paid as a single lump sum (note; Administration Act s 24A). $500 is indexed (Sch 4 cl 2 item 7B).
-- (1A) where both members of a couple have it on the first day under a s 28 or 29 determination: each gets $500 multiplied by
-- their percentage under the determination.
-- (2) not if another individual "has received an amount under this section in respect of that child while the individual and the
-- other individual were members of the same couple". (4) "cannot receive more than one amount" per FTB child.
-- So the upfront payment follows the supplement: no newborn supplement (for example because parental leave pay is payable,
-- cl 35A(8)), no upfront payment.
GIVEN `supplement added` IS A BOOLEAN, `partner already received it` IS A BOOLEAN, `already received it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the newborn upfront payment is payable` IF
    `supplement added` AND (NOT `partner already received it`) AND (NOT `already received it`)

GIVEN `upfront amount` IS A NUMBER, `percentage under the determination` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the shared newborn upfront payment` MEANS
    `upfront amount` TIMES `percentage under the determination` DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `Sch 2 cll 11, 12 -- subsidised hours (the activity test)`

-- cl 11(1)(a): the subsidised hours for a CCS fortnight are "the highest of (i) the 3 day guarantee ... and (ii) any other result"
-- in the table in (1B); (b) for a member of a couple, "the lower of" the individual's and the partner's results.
-- (1A) "The 3 day guarantee for an individual for a CCS fortnight, in relation to any child, is 72."
-- cl 12(1) "The increased hours result is 100." (1A) it applies "if the individual engages in more than 48 hours of a recognised
-- participation type in the CCS fortnight" -- paid work, training, approved study, or prescribed or determined types.
-- Other results (Minister's rules, child wellbeing 100, exceptional circumstances, Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander child 100)
-- are an input here, 0 if none.
GIVEN `participation hours in the fortnight` IS A NUMBER, `other result` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the individual's own subsidised hours` MEANS
    `the larger of`
        (IF `participation hours in the fortnight` GREATER THAN 48 THEN 100 ELSE 72)
        `other result`

GIVEN `my participation hours` IS A NUMBER, `partner participation hours` IS A NUMBER, `in a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the subsidised hours for the fortnight` MEANS
    IF `in a couple`
    THEN `the smaller of` (`the individual's own subsidised hours` `my participation hours` 0)
                          (`the individual's own subsidised hours` `partner participation hours` 0)
    ELSE `the individual's own subsidised hours` `my participation hours` 0

GIVEN `days a week` IS A NUMBER, `hours a day` IS A NUMBER, `subsidised hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every hour of care in the fortnight is within the subsidised hours` IF
    `days a week` TIMES `hours a day` TIMES 2 AT MOST `subsidised hours`

§§ `Sch 2 cll 2, 3 -- the applicable percentage and the hourly rate`

-- cl 3(1) table: adjusted taxable income "equal to or below the lower income (base rate) threshold" -- 90%; "above the lower ...
-- and below the upper" -- see subclause (2) [a formula, absent from the deposit]; "equal to or above the upper" -- 0%.
-- (4) "lower income (base rate) threshold means $80,000" (indexed annually: Sch 4 cl 2 item 18); "upper income (base rate)
-- threshold means the lower income (base rate) threshold plus $450,000" (the $450,000 is not listed as indexed).
-- cl 2(1): the hourly rate of CCS is the applicable percentage "of the lower of (a) the hourly session fee ... and (b) the CCS hourly
-- rate cap", rounded to the nearest cent. (3) cap for a centre-based day care service: printed $11.98, which "reflect[s] the
-- indexation applied on 1 July 2019". Rounding is not encoded; the cases use figures that need none.
GIVEN `income` IS A NUMBER, `lower threshold` IS A NUMBER, `taper result` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the applicable percentage` MEANS
    IF `income` AT MOST `lower threshold`
    THEN 90
    ELSE IF `income` AT LEAST `lower threshold` PLUS 450000
         THEN 0
         ELSE `taper result`

GIVEN `percentage` IS A NUMBER, `hourly session fee` IS A NUMBER, `hourly rate cap` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the hourly rate of CCS` MEANS
    `percentage` TIMES (`the smaller of` `hourly session fee` `hourly rate cap`) DIVIDED BY 100
